{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold now, this city.</b> It is difficult: whichever way you take it — if the city had already been condemned, what does his request from them accomplish? And further, it appears to me that they heeded his voice and said <b>I have accepted your face</b> etc. — but if it had not been condemned, then even without Lot's request they have no permission to destroy it." "<b>Rather,</b> the matter may be explained along the lines of what they said in tractate Shabbat (10a): Zoar was settled fifty-one years and Sodom fifty-two, etc., end of quotation. According to this, Lot judged before them that its measure had not yet been completed. And it is true that the law changes (Bava Kamma 60a) between before permission is granted to the destroyer and after it is granted etc. — for even though its measure had not yet been completed, once permission has been given to the destroyer it has no merit to escape the judgment. And according to this, the matter depends on the destroyer's hand; therefore Lot acted wisely and asked the thing from him, and he accepted his words and said <b>I have accepted your face</b> etc. And you will find that Lot immediately departed from Zoar, because he feared that the time for the completion of its punishment had arrived."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:24.953052175Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}